--commands.verbose:`/chat:verbose`: whether the chat shows each tool call.
--commands.write:`/learn`: a skill written from what it just did, where it may write `skills/` with its file tool.
--connections.activity:How each tool it calls shows, a line each with what it works on (`› file read: notes/plan.md`, `› run command: cargo test`), where its harness tells its calls (ACP'\''s `tool_call`), as Link Harness does: `replace`, above the answer being written, the latest eight, the finished answer then shown alone; `keep`, the same, every line staying above the finished answer as a log; or `off`, none. Link'\''s specification sets `replace`; `/chat:verbose` turns it off and on for one conversation.
--connections.activity_mark:What leads each tool call'\''s line (`"›"`): empty (`""`), nothing. Link'\''s specification sets `"›"`.
--connections.activity_separator:What stands between a tool call and what it works on (`": "`), as `› run command: git commit`; a call with nothing to show it works on shows none (`› web search`). Link'\''s specification sets `": "`.
--connections.ask_wait:How long a question for you waits for your answer, a call of a tool that asks first or a page to open, a second to a day: no answer in time is no, and a tool'\''s call has its own `timeout` beside it. `[connections]`'\''s alone, since a question waits as long on every connection. Link'\''s specification sets `"10m"`.
--connections.cache:How long its provider'\''s cache is asked to keep a conversation'\''s prompt: `"auto"`, the lifetime expected to cost least, or one the provider offers (`"1h"`). Link'\''s specification sets `"auto"`.
--connections.compact_after:When a quiet conversation on it is compacted by time: `"auto"`, just before its cache ends when that costs less than reading it again; a time of quiet, at least `"1m"`; or `"never"`. It needs the `scheduler` tool. Link'\''s specification sets `"auto"`, and `"never"` for `link`.
--connections.documents:Whether a message'\''s documents (PDF or text) reach the agent; false or left out, each is left out and the agent told so.
--connections.groups:Which of the owner'\''s messages in a group an agent answers. `mention`, those that mention it, or answer one of its messages; `never`, none: it talks in direct messages only.
--connections.images:Whether a message'\''s images reach the agent; false or left out, each is left out and the agent told so.
--connections.pace:How often an answer being written is shown again, over 0; never more often than the platform documents a bot may write: Telegram once a second in a chat and every 3 seconds in a group, Slack every 1.2 seconds, and Discord its global 50 requests a second and the limits it answers with. Told by the platform to wait, Telegram and Slack show nothing more until then, and only the finished answer waits and tries again. Link'\''s specification sets `"1s"`.
--connections.pauses:What `"auto"` assumes of a new conversation'\''s pauses, each counted as one it saw. Link'\''s specification sets a chat'\''s to `["1m", "1m", "20m", "8h"]`.
--connections.steered:A reaction on a message that joined a running turn ([`Busy::Steer`]), where the connection has them; empty (`""`) or left out, none.
--connections.stream:The answer shown as it'\''s written; false, once it'\''s done. Link'\''s specification sets true.
--connections.voice:Whether a message'\''s voice notes reach the agent, heard as their words by its provider (`[model] transcribe`); false or left out, each is left out and the agent told so.
--connections.working:A reaction on your message while it answers, by its name (`"eyes"`), where the connection has them; empty (`""`) or left out, none. Of Link'\''s connections Slack and Discord mark a message, so it'\''s refused for Telegram and Signal; Discord knows the names its `reactions.toml` lists. Link'\''s `[connection.slack]` and `[connection.discord]` set `"eyes"`.
--env:Environment input for future agent creation, relative to this file.
