--settings.agent.access.message:Who may message the agent, besides its owner: chats on its connections, whoever is in them, each `chat:<connection>:<chat id>` (`chat:slack:C0TEAM`).
--settings.agent.command_response:Text shown before a command'\''s harness answer; empty disables it.
--settings.agent.commands.ask:`/chat:ask`: a question answered apart, nothing kept.
--settings.agent.commands.compact:`/chat:compact`: what'\''s before the last message summarized now.
--settings.agent.commands.create:`/new`: a new conversation in the same chat.
--settings.agent.commands.export:`/chat:export`: this conversation written to a file.
--settings.agent.commands.fork:`/chat:fork`: a conversation holding this one as it stands.
--settings.agent.commands.goal:`/goal`: a goal it pursues after each answer until it holds, within `[goals]`'\'' limits.
--settings.agent.commands.help:`/help`: the commands that are on.
--settings.agent.commands.model:`/model`: the model, or a switch to another of its provider'\''s.
--settings.agent.commands.models:`/models`: the models offered by its provider.
--settings.agent.commands.queue:`/chat:queue`: the next message waits for the running turn.
--settings.agent.commands.rename:`/chat:rename`: this conversation'\''s name.
--settings.agent.commands.resume:`/chat:resume`: the chat'\''s conversations, or one taken up again.
--settings.agent.commands.skills:`/skill:list`, and each skill run as `/skill:<name>`.
--settings.agent.commands.status:`/status`: the model and what the conversation holds.
--settings.agent.commands.steer:`/chat:steer`: the next message joins the running turn, where `[turns] busy` steers.
--settings.agent.commands.stop:`/stop`: the answer being written stopped.
--settings.agent.commands.tasks:`/tasks` and `/ps`: its running and scheduled work.
--settings.agent.commands.verbose:`/chat:verbose`: whether the chat shows each tool call.
--settings.agent.commands.write:`/learn`: a skill written from what it just did, where it may write `skills/` with its file tool.
--settings.agent.connections.activity:How each tool it calls shows, a line each with what it works on (`› file read: notes/plan.md`, `› run command: cargo test`), where its harness tells its calls (ACP'\''s `tool_call`), as Link Harness does: `replace`, above the answer being written, the latest eight, the finished answer then shown alone; `keep`, the same, every line staying above the finished answer as a log; or `off`, none. Link'\''s specification sets `replace`; `/chat:verbose` turns it off and on for one conversation.
--settings.agent.connections.activity_mark:What leads each tool call'\''s line (`"›"`): empty (`""`), nothing. Link'\''s specification sets `"›"`.
--settings.agent.connections.activity_separator:What stands between a tool call and what it works on (`": "`), as `› run command: git commit`; a call with nothing to show it works on shows none (`› web search`). Link'\''s specification sets `": "`.
--settings.agent.connections.ask_wait:How long a question for you waits for your answer, a call of a tool that asks first or a page to open, a second to a day: no answer in time is no, and a tool'\''s call has its own `timeout` beside it. `[connections]`'\''s alone, since a question waits as long on every connection. Link'\''s specification sets `"10m"`.
--settings.agent.connections.cache:How long its provider'\''s cache is asked to keep a conversation'\''s prompt: `"auto"`, the lifetime expected to cost least, or one the provider offers (`"1h"`). Link'\''s specification sets `"auto"`.
--settings.agent.connections.compact_after:When a quiet conversation on it is compacted by time: `"auto"`, just before its cache ends when that costs less than reading it again; a time of quiet, at least `"1m"`; or `"never"`. It needs the `scheduler` tool. Link'\''s specification sets `"auto"`, and `"never"` for `link`.
--settings.agent.connections.documents:Whether a message'\''s documents (PDF or text) reach the agent; false or left out, each is left out and the agent told so.
--settings.agent.connections.groups:Which of the owner'\''s messages in a group an agent answers. `mention`, those that mention it, or answer one of its messages; `never`, none: it talks in direct messages only.
--settings.agent.connections.images:Whether a message'\''s images reach the agent; false or left out, each is left out and the agent told so.
--settings.agent.connections.pace:How often an answer being written is shown again, over 0; never more often than the platform documents a bot may write: Telegram once a second in a chat and every 3 seconds in a group, Slack every 1.2 seconds, and Discord its global 50 requests a second and the limits it answers with. Told by the platform to wait, Telegram and Slack show nothing more until then, and only the finished answer waits and tries again. Link'\''s specification sets `"1s"`.
--settings.agent.connections.pauses:What `"auto"` assumes of a new conversation'\''s pauses, each counted as one it saw. Link'\''s specification sets a chat'\''s to `["1m", "1m", "20m", "8h"]`.
--settings.agent.connections.steered:A reaction on a message that joined a running turn ([`Busy::Steer`]), where the connection has them; empty (`""`) or left out, none.
--settings.agent.connections.stream:The answer shown as it'\''s written; false, once it'\''s done. Link'\''s specification sets true.
--settings.agent.connections.voice:Whether a message'\''s voice notes reach the agent, heard as their words by its provider (`[model] transcribe`); false or left out, each is left out and the agent told so.
--settings.agent.connections.working:A reaction on your message while it answers, by its name (`"eyes"`), where the connection has them; empty (`""`) or left out, none. Of Link'\''s connections Slack and Discord mark a message, so it'\''s refused for Telegram and Signal; Discord knows the names its `reactions.toml` lists. Link'\''s `[connection.slack]` and `[connection.discord]` set `"eyes"`.
--settings.agent.env:Environment input for future agent creation, relative to this file.
--settings.agent.extends:What a specification starts from. `link`, link'\''s specification, as when it'\''s left out; `none`, nothing: every key is the file'\''s own.
--settings.agent.goals.tokens:The most tokens those turns spend, its prompts'\'' and answers'\'', at least 1000: Link'\''s specification sets 1000000.
--settings.agent.goals.turns:The most turns it takes on its own toward a goal, after the one that set it, from 1 to 1000. Link'\''s specification sets 10.
--settings.agent.harness:The harness'\''s name, as `lnk agent harness list` names it (`link`, `openclaw`): lowercase letters, digits and dashes.
--settings.agent.harness.name:The harness'\''s name, as `lnk agent harness list` names it (`link`, `openclaw`): lowercase letters, digits and dashes.
--settings.agent.instructions.base:The prompt'\''s first section, what any agent of yours is: `link` (Link'\''s, a personal agent who answers briefly), `none`, or a file in its files (`instructions/base.md`). Link'\''s specification sets `"link"`.
--settings.agent.instructions.environment:The fourth section, what it runs with here as Link resolved it at its start: where its files are, which folders it may change, its connections; `link`, `none` or a file. Link'\''s specification sets `"link"`.
--settings.agent.instructions.max.base:The base section: its most (`"16 KB"`), past which it'\''s cut.
--settings.agent.instructions.max.environment:What it runs with here: its most (`"16 KB"`), past which it'\''s cut.
--settings.agent.instructions.max.model:The model'\''s own section, the second, from `instructions/models/<maker>/<model>/instruction.md` in its files: its most, past which it'\''s cut. It has no source key.
--settings.agent.instructions.max.notes:What the agent noted for itself: its most (`"16 KB"`), past which it'\''s cut.
--settings.agent.instructions.max.now:The date, connection and speaker at the head of each message: its most (`"16 KB"`), past which it'\''s cut.
--settings.agent.instructions.max.owner:Who its owner is: its most (`"16 KB"`), past which it'\''s cut.
--settings.agent.instructions.max.persona:Who it is: its most (`"16 KB"`), past which it'\''s cut.
--settings.agent.instructions.max.repository:What the repository it works in says of itself: its most (`"16 KB"`), past which it'\''s cut.
--settings.agent.instructions.max.skills:Its skills: its most (`"16 KB"`), past which it'\''s cut.
--settings.agent.instructions.max.standing:What its owner tells it to be: its most (`"16 KB"`), past which it'\''s cut.
--settings.agent.instructions.max.tools:The tools'\'' section, the third, what each tool says of itself: its most, past which tools are cut whole. It has no source key.
--settings.agent.instructions.notes:The ninth section, what the agent noted for itself, the file its memory'\''s `remember` writes, read at each message, or `none`. Link'\''s specification sets `"memory/notes.md"`; the old `instructions/notes.md` reads as it.
--settings.agent.instructions.now:The date, the time here, the connection and who'\''s speaking, at the head of each message, never in the system prompt: `link` or `none`. Link'\''s specification sets `"link"`.
--settings.agent.instructions.owner:The seventh section, who you are (your name, your work, the people in your life, how you like things): a file of yours in its files, read at each message, or `none`. Link'\''s specification sets `"instructions/owner.md"`.
--settings.agent.instructions.persona:The sixth section, who it is apart from any task (its name, its voice, its character): a file of yours in its files, read at each message, or `none`. Link'\''s specification sets `"instructions/persona.md"`.
--settings.agent.instructions.repository:What the repository it works in says of itself: `link` (its `AGENTS.md`, else `CLAUDE.md`, nearest folder first) or `none`. A feature'\''s switch, off when left out.
--settings.agent.instructions.skills:The fifth section, each skill'\''s name and what it'\''s for, from `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` in its files, sorted by name; `link`, `none` or a file. Link'\''s specification sets `"link"`.
--settings.agent.instructions.source:The whole prompt'\''s source: `"link"`, as left out, assembles the sections below; a Markdown file in the agent'\''s files (`"instructions/instruction.md"`) supplies the whole system prompt, read again each turn without headings, templates, model overrides or message times; `"none"` supplies none.
--settings.agent.instructions.standing:The eighth section, your standing instructions: a file in its files it may edit, read at each message, or `none`. Link'\''s specification sets `"instructions/instruction.md"`.
--settings.agent.isolation.vm:The VM specification a new agent is made in, relative to this file. This build has no VM provider, so a specification naming one is refused, never run in a sandbox instead.
--settings.agent.model.allow:The only models it may run; left out, any.
--settings.agent.model.answer:The longest answer, in tokens, as you set it, at least 256; left out, `[window] answer`'\''s share of the window, at most the model'\''s own.
--settings.agent.model.anthropic.allow:The only models of this provider it may run; left out, `[model]`'\''s.
--settings.agent.model.anthropic.answer:The longest answer, in tokens, at least 256.
--settings.agent.model.anthropic.default:The model when the agent names none, as this provider names it (`claude-sonnet-5-5`).
--settings.agent.model.anthropic.thinking:How hard a model thinks: `off`, `low`, `medium` or `high`.
--settings.agent.model.anthropic.thinking_budget:The most tokens it thinks, at least 1024, for a model that thinks within a budget.
--settings.agent.model.anthropic.transcribe:The model of this provider a voice note is heard with; `"none"`, none.
--settings.agent.model.default:The model when the agent names none.
--settings.agent.model.fallback:Whether a turn its model can'\''t answer goes to the fallback model, `fallback_model`: the model is off, the turn'\''s prompt is past its window, or its provider is busy (429, or a 5xx). False, it fails, and the agent keeps no fallback.
--settings.agent.model.fallback_model:The hosted model used when falling back, named as `default` names one (`anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5`), or one of `aliases`. Its credential is its provider'\''s, or `LNK_FALLBACK_CREDENTIAL`'\''s. Link Harness falls back; a harness that can'\''t says so.
--settings.agent.model.local.allow:The only models of this provider it may run; left out, `[model]`'\''s.
--settings.agent.model.local.answer:The longest answer, in tokens, at least 256.
--settings.agent.model.local.default:The model when the agent names none, as this provider names it (`claude-sonnet-5-5`).
--settings.agent.model.local.thinking:How hard a model thinks: `off`, `low`, `medium` or `high`.
--settings.agent.model.local.thinking_budget:The most tokens it thinks, at least 1024, for a model that thinks within a budget.
--settings.agent.model.local.transcribe:The model of this provider a voice note is heard with; `"none"`, none.
--settings.agent.model.ollama.allow:The only models of this provider it may run; left out, `[model]`'\''s.
--settings.agent.model.ollama.answer:The longest answer, in tokens, at least 256.
--settings.agent.model.ollama.default:The model when the agent names none, as this provider names it (`claude-sonnet-5-5`).
--settings.agent.model.ollama.thinking:How hard a model thinks: `off`, `low`, `medium` or `high`.
--settings.agent.model.ollama.thinking_budget:The most tokens it thinks, at least 1024, for a model that thinks within a budget.
--settings.agent.model.ollama.transcribe:The model of this provider a voice note is heard with; `"none"`, none.
--settings.agent.model.openai.allow:The only models of this provider it may run; left out, `[model]`'\''s.
--settings.agent.model.openai.answer:The longest answer, in tokens, at least 256.
--settings.agent.model.openai.default:The model when the agent names none, as this provider names it (`claude-sonnet-5-5`).
--settings.agent.model.openai.thinking:How hard a model thinks: `off`, `low`, `medium` or `high`.
--settings.agent.model.openai.thinking_budget:The most tokens it thinks, at least 1024, for a model that thinks within a budget.
--settings.agent.model.openai.transcribe:The model of this provider a voice note is heard with; `"none"`, none.
--settings.agent.model.openrouter.allow:The only models of this provider it may run; left out, `[model]`'\''s.
--settings.agent.model.openrouter.answer:The longest answer, in tokens, at least 256.
--settings.agent.model.openrouter.default:The model when the agent names none, as this provider names it (`claude-sonnet-5-5`).
--settings.agent.model.openrouter.thinking:How hard a model thinks: `off`, `low`, `medium` or `high`.
--settings.agent.model.openrouter.thinking_budget:The most tokens it thinks, at least 1024, for a model that thinks within a budget.
--settings.agent.model.openrouter.transcribe:The model of this provider a voice note is heard with; `"none"`, none.
--settings.agent.model.thinking:How hard a model thinks: `off`, `low`, `medium` or `high`.
--settings.agent.model.thinking_budget:The most tokens it thinks, at least 1024, for a model that thinks within a budget. Link'\''s specification sets 2048.
--settings.agent.model.transcribe:The model of its provider a voice note is heard with, its words the message'\''s (`[connections] voice`); left out, or `"none"`, a voice note is left out, and the agent told so. Link'\''s specification sets OpenAI'\''s `gpt-4o-mini-transcribe`.
--settings.agent.name:The agent'\''s own name, no other: lowercase letters, digits and dashes. A specification naming another agent is refused.
--settings.agent.run.files:The agent'\''s workspace folder. A relative path is from the folder the start runs in; left out, it keeps the workspace it has. `lnk agent start --run.files <dir>` sets it.
--settings.agent.run.idle_after:How long it goes with no message, no turn and no background command before it stops, holding no process, memory or port, started again by its next message: at least `"1s"`, or `"never"`, memory kept against a start from cold. Link'\''s specification sets `"5m"`.
--settings.agent.run.let_sleep:Whether the machine may sleep while this agent runs: left out or false, the agent keeps it awake; true, the machine'\''s own sleep policy applies.
--settings.agent.schedules:Schedule definitions owned by this agent, independent of its harness.
--settings.agent.storage.conversations:Where a new conversation is kept: a place (`file` or a driver'\''s name, `sqlite` the program `lnk-sqlite-store`, a store), or `log` or `compact`, each `file`. A conversation already kept is read where it is: `lnk agent chat export --format` converts it.
--settings.agent.storage.home:Where it would keep its home, the person'\''s documents and work (`Home/`): a place'\''s name, lowercase letters, digits and dashes. It'\''s a request: the machine'\''s `[storage]` has the last word, and a place it doesn'\''t support gets its default. Link'\''s specification sets `"file"`.
--settings.agent.storage.instructions:Where it would keep its instructions, which you edit. It'\''s a request: the machine'\''s `[storage]` has the last word, and a place it doesn'\''t support gets its default. Link'\''s specification sets `"file"`.
--settings.agent.storage.memory:Where it would keep memory'\''s notes and index. It'\''s a request: the machine'\''s `[storage]` has the last word, and a place it doesn'\''t support gets its default. Link'\''s specification sets `"file"`.
--settings.agent.storage.schedule:Where it would keep its scheduled jobs. It'\''s a request: the machine'\''s `[storage]` has the last word, and a place it doesn'\''t support gets its default. Link'\''s specification sets `"file"`.
--settings.agent.storage.skills:Where it would keep its skills, which you edit. It'\''s a request: the machine'\''s `[storage]` has the last word, and a place it doesn'\''t support gets its default. Link'\''s specification sets `"file"`.
--settings.agent.tools.answer:What'\''s kept of a tool'\''s answer, 1 KB to 16 MB; in `[tool.<name>]`, one tool'\''s. Link'\''s specification sets `"32 KB"`.
--settings.agent.tools.ask:The scheduler'\''s: whether every call but those that only read asks you first. A recurring schedule asks you either way, unless its call says once or `recurring` is `allow`. Link'\''s specification sets false.
--settings.agent.tools.background:Run'\''s: the most background commands at once, 0 to 64; 0, none. Link'\''s specification sets 4.
--settings.agent.tools.background_keep:Run'\''s: how long a background command'\''s record and output stay once it ended and the agent was told, 1m to 365d. Link'\''s specification sets `"1d"`.
--settings.agent.tools.background_output:Run'\''s: what'\''s kept on disk of a background command'\''s output, its end, 1 KB to 1 GB. Link'\''s specification sets `"16 MB"`.
--settings.agent.tools.background_per_day:Run'\''s: the most background commands started in a day, each of whose endings starts a turn, 1 to 65535. Link'\''s specification sets 100.
--settings.agent.tools.background_timeout:Run'\''s: the longest a background command runs before it'\''s stopped, 1s to 7d. Link'\''s specification sets `"1h"`.
--settings.agent.tools.deadline:Memory'\''s: how long a search ranks before it answers with what it has. Link'\''s specification sets `"300ms"`.
--settings.agent.tools.diffs:File'\''s: whether `write` and `replace` answer with the change as a diff. A feature'\''s switch, off when left out.
--settings.agent.tools.dimensions:Memory'\''s: how many of the embedding model'\''s dimensions are kept: fewer cost less memory and disk, more rank a little better. Link'\''s specification sets 256.
--settings.agent.tools.driver:What wakes the scheduler'\''s runner. `service`, the agent'\''s bridge, a background service, runs it for good; `cron`, the machine'\''s calendar (launchd on a mac, cron elsewhere) starts it once a minute; nothing of it runs between; `address`, a machine that runs the agent only while it answers: the scheduler tells it, at the address the machine gives, when the agent'\''s jobs are next due, and whatever wakes the agent then runs it once; nothing of it runs between.
--settings.agent.tools.enabled:Whether Link starts the tool for the agent, in `[tool.scheduler]`, `[tool.run]`, `[tool.file]`, `[tool.code]` and `[tool.mcp]`; false withholds it. Link'\''s specification starts the file tool enabled, and the scheduler, run, code and Link MCP disabled. Without the scheduler, no subagents or schedules run. `[tool.browser]` and `[tool.desktop]` take it too: true gives the screen at a start where this machine runs it, false takes it away, and Link'\''s specification says neither, leaving what `lnk agent tool add` gave.
--settings.agent.tools.fetch:Web'\''s: the most of a page one fetch gives, 1 KB to 1 MB; each part says where the next starts. Link'\''s specification sets `"24 KB"`.
--settings.agent.tools.file:Memory'\''s: the largest file in its folders it indexes; a larger one is left out, and a search'\''s reply names it. Link'\''s specification sets `"16 MB"`.
--settings.agent.tools.find:File'\''s: whether it finds files by name and lines by a pattern (`find`). A feature'\''s switch, off when left out.
--settings.agent.tools.firing:The scheduler'\''s: how long it waits on a firing, a subagent'\''s whole work, before it gives up on it, 1s to 1d. Link'\''s specification sets `"30m"`.
--settings.agent.tools.folders:Memory'\''s: the agent'\''s folders it indexes, `memory` (its Home'\''s) and `chats` (its conversations). Link'\''s specification sets both.
--settings.agent.tools.hops:The scheduler'\''s: how deep a chain of messages goes, each sent by an agent on its own, from 1: a depth and not a count, as a recurring job'\''s firings start again. Link'\''s specification sets 8.
--settings.agent.tools.hosts:Web'\''s: the only hosts it fetches, as `[internet] hosts` names them: a name (`docs.rs`), `*.` and a name for every name under it, or an address; each redirect is held to them too. Left out, it fetches any public host, as Link'\''s specification leaves it. Link Harness sends it with each call.
--settings.agent.tools.interval:The scheduler'\''s: the shortest a recurring schedule may repeat, 1m to 1d; a model'\''s `cron` that fires more often is refused when it'\''s made. Link'\''s specification sets `"5m"`.
--settings.agent.tools.keep:Memory'\''s: how long its session stays once no turn uses it. Link'\''s specification sets `"10m"`.
--settings.agent.tools.kept_off:Memory'\''s: the largest index kept off the machine, fetched at each wake where the machine runs agents only while they answer. Link'\''s specification sets `"2 GB"`.
--settings.agent.tools.late:What a firing missed while the machine slept does. `run`, it fires once, on waking; `skip`, it doesn'\''t; a recurring one fires at its next time.
--settings.agent.tools.max_age:Memory'\''s: how long its session lives at most. Link'\''s specification sets `"1h"`.
--settings.agent.tools.memory:Memory'\''s: the most its service holds of its own for this agent'\''s index, besides the pages of files it maps. Link'\''s specification sets `"512 MB"`.
--settings.agent.tools.model:Memory'\''s: the embedding model it ranks by; `none`, by words only, no model started. Link'\''s specification sets `qwen3-embedding`.
--settings.agent.tools.notes:Memory'\''s: how large the agent'\''s notes may grow, 64 B to 64 KB, past which `remember` refuses to write. Link'\''s specification sets `"4 KB"`.
--settings.agent.tools.output:Run'\''s: what'\''s kept of each of a command'\''s output and its errors, its start and its end, 1 KB to 16 MB. Link'\''s specification sets `"16 KB"`.
--settings.agent.tools.per_day:The scheduler'\''s: messages its schedules send the agent a day, the day in its `zone`, from 1; subagents'\'' work is outside it. It bounds how many messages agents send each other, and caps what the agent takes from each teammate a day (UTC). Link'\''s specification sets 100.
--settings.agent.tools.program:The browser'\''s: the Chromium-family program it starts, by its absolute path, in place of the one it finds on this machine. It'\''s an executable program, never a launcher script (a file starting with `#!`), which would run inside the browser'\''s sandbox and be refused the programs it calls; each start checks it, and refuses one that isn'\''t. Left out, the browser finds one, as Link'\''s specification leaves it.
--settings.agent.tools.recurring:The scheduler'\''s: whether a recurring schedule the agent makes asks you first. `ask`, it waits for you to allow it unless its call says once; `allow`, it starts without asking, as a one-off reminder does, though `ask = true` still asks first of every call that writes. Link'\''s specification sets `ask`.
--settings.agent.tools.reserve:Memory'\''s: the disk left free; below it indexing pauses, calls go on answering, and it resumes once there'\''s room. Link'\''s specification sets `"1 GB"`.
--settings.agent.tools.strangers:`[tools]` only: the tools a stranger'\''s message may use, by the names the harness offers them (`web__fetch`), its conversation given these or fewer ([`crate::access::Standing::Stranger`]). Left out, none.
--settings.agent.tools.subagents:The scheduler'\''s: subagents at work at once, from 1. Link'\''s specification sets 5.
--settings.agent.tools.threads:Memory'\''s: the threads indexing takes, so a laptop isn'\''t taken over. Link'\''s specification sets 1.
--settings.agent.tools.timeout:How long a tool'\''s call may take, at least a second; past it the model is told it didn'\''t answer. In `[tool.<name>]`, one tool'\''s: the run tool stops a command a tenth before it (2 s at least, half at most), with all it started, so what it printed comes back. Waiting for you to allow a call isn'\''t counted: a tool not Link'\''s own has `[connections] ask_wait` beside it. Link'\''s specification sets `"5m"`, and the run tool'\''s `"2m"`.
--settings.agent.tools.tokens:Memory'\''s: the most tokens a search or a read gives, at least 100 and at most 6000, the most one answer holds. Link'\''s specification sets 6000.
--settings.agent.tools.zone:The scheduler'\''s: the time zone its times are in, `local` (this machine'\''s) or a zone'\''s name (`Europe/Paris`). Link'\''s specification sets `local`.
--settings.agent.turns.busy:What a message sent while a turn runs does. `queue`, it gets a turn of its own after; `steer`, it joins the running turn, at its next round; `interrupt`, the running turn ends now, and it gets a turn of its own.
--settings.agent.turns.calls:The most calls one answer makes, from 1. Link'\''s specification sets 16.
--settings.agent.turns.lapse:How long a lease not renewed lasts before its turn is taken for crashed and finished, more than twice `renew`. Link'\''s specification sets `"60s"`.
--settings.agent.turns.renew:How often a running turn renews its lease, at least `"1s"`. Link'\''s specification sets `"10s"`.
--settings.agent.turns.rounds:The most rounds of calls in one turn, from 1. Link'\''s specification sets 8.
--settings.agent.version:A whole number of yours, to say which revision of the specification this is; Link reads nothing from it.
--settings.agent.window.answer:The share of the window kept for the answer, over 0 and under 1 and under 1 with `margin`, at most the model'\''s longest, where `[model] answer` doesn'\''t say. Link'\''s specification sets 0.25.
--settings.agent.window.compact_at:When a conversation is compacted (`[window] compact_at`): once it fills this share of what the window holds of it, or `never`.
--settings.agent.window.margin:The share of the window kept back, from 0 to under 0.5: tokens are counted roughly before a turn, exactly by the provider after (`0.125`, an eighth). Link'\''s specification sets 0.125.
--settings.agent.window.max:The window a turn fills, in tokens, at least 1024: yours or a team'\''s as set, Link'\''s held to the model'\''s own window; left out, the model'\''s whole window. Link'\''s specification sets 128000.
--settings.agent.window.past_price_jump:Whether a turn fills the window past its model'\''s first price jump, where a long prompt costs more (the model'\''s facts'\'' `above`, as `lnk model show` prints them).
--settings.agent.window.save_notes:Whether, before it compacts, the model is asked to save what matters to its notes, where it has a tool to (`memory__remember`), in a conversation you spoke in, never one of others'\'' messages alone. Link'\''s specification sets true.
--settings.agent.window.unknown:The window of a model Link doesn'\''t know, in tokens, at least 1024. Link'\''s specification sets 32768.
--settings.memory.daily_credits:Shared daily memory spending in credits; required when enabling semantic search. All callers debit the same team budget.
--settings.memory.enabled:Whether the team has a memory over its shared folder, handed to the members granted all of it: off until the owner turns it on (`lnk agent team-memory start`).
--settings.memory.indexer.kind:Which keeper it is: auto, elected, or a named member.
--settings.memory.indexer.member:The member, by its name in the team'\''s file.
--settings.memory.payer.kind:Who pays: the team'\''s owner, or a named member.
--settings.memory.payer.member:The member, by its name in the team'\''s file.
--settings.memory.semantic:Non-indexers use words until the owner enables semantic queries.
